573	|	 	|	0	|	0	|		|	Leishmania hertigi is classified in the subgenus Leishmania and is one\nof the two species in the L. hertigi complex (the other being L. deanei)\nin the 1987 classification ( Evolution, classification and geographical\ndistribution\" p90 in: The Leishmaniases in Biology and Medicine, Volume\n1. Eds. W. Peters and R. Killick-Kendrick 1987).\nHowever, Leishmania hertigi is now regarded as a dubious species of\nLeishmania and the result of recent works suggest that it belongs into\nthe genus Endotrypanum. For the time being it is therefore not\nassigned to any of the Leishmania subgenera or species complexes.	|	47002 	|
