2007	|	Streptomonospora salina	|	0	|	0	|		|	Description of Streptomonospora salina sp. nov. Streptomonospora salina (sa.li na. L. adj. salina, salted, saline). Aerial mycelium is well developed but not fragmented. Colonies are white on most media. Two-type spores with wrinkly surfaces are borne onaerial mycelium and substrate mycelium respectively. No diffusible pigment is produced, but melanin is produced. Streptomonospora salina is positive for melanin and negative for milk coagulation, milk peptonization, starch hydrolysis, H2S production and gelation liquefaction. Optimal growth occurs in media supplemented with salt at concentration of 15% (wt/vol) at 28 and pH 7.0. Isolated from hypersaline habitats (a salt lake in China). The type strain is strain YIM90002T.	|	104205 	|
