11056	|	Halobacteria	|	0	|	0	|		|	From a nomenclatural standpoint, Halobacteria Grant et al. 2002 is a junior homotypic synonym of Halomebacteria Cavalier-Smith 2002, as both have the type order Halobacteriales. However, Cavalier-Smith includes the Methanosarcinales in the class Halomebacteria. In contrast, Grant et al. do not include the Methanosarcinales in the class Halobacteria. The nomenclatural form that is most consistent with the taxonomic outline used in the GenBank Taxonomy Database is here given priority.	|	94695 183963 	|
11057	|	Methanococci & Methanothermea	|	0	|	0	|		|	From a nomenclatural standpoint, Methanococci Boone 2002 may be considered a junior homotypic synonym of Methanothermea Cavalier-Smith 2002, as both have the type order Methanococcales. However, Cavalier-Smith includes the Methanosarcinales in the class Halobacteria. In contrast, Boone includes the Methanosarcinales in the class Methanococci. Neither circumscription is consistent with unpublished analyses of complete genome data (C. Woese, personal communication). In version 4.0  of the BMSB Taxonomic Outline, the class 'Methanobicrobia' was created to include the orders Methanomicrobiales and Methanosaricnales.	|	183939 224756 	|
