11669	|	Glaphyromorphus arnhemicus:	|	0	|	0	|	 	|	The taxonomic status of Glaphyromorphus arnhemicus is underdiscussion. The most recent edition of Harold Cogger's \"Reptiles andAmphibians of Australia\" (2000) lists Glaphyromorphus arnhemicus as asubspecies of Glaphyromorphus darwinensis, Paul Horner's \"Skinks ofthe Northern Territory\" (1991) lists it as a subspecies ofGlaphyromorphus crassicaudus, and Allen Greer's \"The Biology andEvolution of Australian Lizards\" (1989) recognized Glaphyromorphusarnhemicus as a full species. Because of morphological differencesbetween the tree taxa, their allopatric distribution, and the lack ofadditional taxonomic work on this group since the 1989 publication,Glaphyromorphus arnhemicus is best treated as separate species untilfurther studies can be completed. (Tod W. Reeder pers. com.)	|	221263 	|
