11883	|	Sinorhizobium = Ensifer	|	0	|	0	|		|	The genus Ensifer is considered a senior synonym of Sinorhizobium by the Judicial Commission of the Interntational Committee on Systematics of Prokaryotes (Judicial Opinion 84).  However, the Subcommittee on the Taxonomy of Agrobacterium and Rhizobium raised strong opposition to this decision at its 2008 meeting in Gent, Belgium (Lindstrom and Young, 2009), to which Young (2010) has responded. Kumar et al. (2017) argue for the merging of the genera, but more recently, Kuzmanovic et al. (2022) provide evidence for the separation of the two genera as distinctly different.  Given the contentious nature of the issue, the NCBI Taxonomy Database retains both genus names for use by submitters in the naming of novel species. For some pre-existing species names, priority in the Database is given to the original form of the validly published name (Sinorhizobium <species> OR Ensifer <species>).	|	28105 106591 227292 	|
