14835	|	Synonymy (Leucoagaricus meleagris)	|	0	|	0	|		|	Leucoagaricus meleagris was originally described by Sowerby in 1798.  It was later transfered to Leucoagaricus (Singer, Lilloa 22: 422, 1952).  Then in 1988 it was transferred to Leucocoprinus (Zschieschang, Mykologisches Mitteilungsblatt 31: 5, 1988).  A recent study of the Agaricaceae (Vellinga 2004) has shown that neither Leucoagaricus nor Leucocoprinus are monophyletic but together, along with Sericeomyces form a monophyletic grouping.  Vellinga found Leucoagaricus meleagris in this large clade containing Leucoagaricus, Leucocoprinus, and  Sericeomyces and sister to Leucoagaricus americanus.	|	201219 	|
