18578	|	Sphingobacteriales genera incertae sedis	|	0	|	0	|		|	In the taxonomic outline of Bergey's Manual of Systematic Bacteriology (second edition), the family Crenotrichaceae Hansgirg 1888 is placed in the order Sphingobacteriales, phylum Bacteroidetes.  However, Stoecker et al. (2006) provide molecular evidence that the genus Crenothrix is more properly placed in the order Methylococcales, phylum Proteobacteria.  Movement of the genus Crenothrix to Methylococcales requires that the family Crenotrichaceae also be moved, as Crenothrix is the type genus of this family.  Consequently, other genera originally assigned to the family Crenotrichaceae and properly belonging to the order Sphingobacteriales(genera Chitinophaga, Rhodothermus, Salinibacter) are now provisionally placed herein under the heading 'Sphingobacteriales genera incertae sedis' pending reassignment to an approproprate family within the order.	|	422177 	|
