20095	|	Bitner (personal communication)	|	0	|	0	|	http://www.paleo.pan.pl	|	In 1959 G.A. Cooper assigned the Recent species Rhynchonella grayi Woodward, 1855 to the fossil Eocene genus Eohemithiris Hertlein & Grant, 1944 known only from California. Later d'Hondt (1987) created a new genus and species, Basiliolella ferox for the material from off southern New Caledonia. Based on the very rich material collected around New Caledonia and the Chesterfield Islands Laurin (1997) concluded that so-called Eohemithiris grayi and Basiliolella ferox are certainly identical, and he synonymized both species. Further investigations (Savage et al. 2002) have shown that Cooper's assignment of R. grayi to Eohemithiris was incorrect and that this species should be attributed to the genus Basiliolella created by d'Hondt. As B. grayi and B. ferox are synonymous (the fact confirmed also by my own examination of the material) the specific name grayi has priority over the name ferox. \n\nCooper, G.A. 1959. Genera of Tertiary and Recent rhynchonelloid brachiopods. Smithsonian Miscellaneous Collections 139 (5): 1-90. \n\nd'Hondt J.-L. 1987. Observations sur les Brachiopodes actuels de Nouvelle Caledonie et d'autres localites de l'Indo-Pacifique. Bulletin du Museum d'Histoire Naturelle, Paris, 4 ser., 9, section A, n. 1, 33-46 \n\nLaurin B. 1997. Brachiopodes recoltes dans les eaux de la Nouvelle Caledonie et des les Loyaute, Matthew et Chesterfield, in CROSNIER A. (ed.), Resultats des Campagnes MUSORSTOM, vol. 18. Memoires du Museum national d'Histoire naturelle 176: 411-471. \n\nSavage, N.M., Mancenido, M.O., Owen, E.F. & Dagys, A.S. 2002. Pugnacoidea. In: Kaesler, R. L. (ed.), Rhyncholelliformea (part). Treatise on Invertebrate Paleontology. Part H. Brachiopoda Revised. Geological Society of America and University of Kansas. Boulder, Colorado and Lawrence, Kansas, vol. 4: 1165-1218. \n\nDr Maria Aleksandra Bitner \nInstitute of Paleobiology \nPolish Academy of Sciences \nul. Twarda 51/55 \n00-818 Warszawa, Poland \ntel. 48-22 697 88 70 \nfax. 48-22 620 62 25	|	1475339 	|
