23530	|	polyphyletic taxon	|	0	|	0	|		|	This taxon is polyphyletic, i.e., it represents an artificial grouping without a single common ancestor. Most polyphyletic taxa have simple morphology and thus are difficult to classify by traditional means. Molecular data have proven to be a valuable tool for detecting phylogenetic patterns in such polyphyletic taxa, which are then classified in different parts of the taxonomy database to better reflect their true relationships.	|	3071 	|
