27175	|	nomenclatural note on Dinema/Dinematomonas 1:	|	0	|	0	|		|	4. Elifa Oezdikmen, Dinema Perty and Dinematomonas Silva (Euglenoidea / Euglenophyceae). \nDinema Perty, 1852 was published as a generic name of euglenids, but the generic name was preoccupied by Dinema Fairmaire, 1849 under ICZN and by Dinema Lindley, 1831 under ICBN. Silva (1960) published a substitute (replacement) name Dinematomonas Silva, and this name is available under ICZN (and valid under ICBN). Therefore, the proposal of a substitute name, Elifa oezdikmen, for Dinema Perty (Oezdikmen, 2009) is invalid (or illegitimate) as an unnecessary junior objective (later homotypic) synonym of Dinematomonas Silva under both ICZN and ICBN. \n\nICZN / ICBN \nDinematomonas Silva, 1960. Taxon, 9. 20. Type species: Dinematomonas griseola (Perty, 1852) based on Dinema griseola Perty, 1852. Synonym: Dinema Perty, 1852 (non Fairmaire, 1849; non Lindley, 1831); Elifa zdikmen, 2009. \n\nfrom: Takashi Nakada (2010). Nomenclatural notes on some ambiregnal generic names (comments to Oezdikmen, 2009). Mun. Ent. Zool. Vol. 5, No. 1, January 2010.	|	181205 181206 	|
