47855	|	gencode:27:Karyorelict Nuclear Code:270	|	0	|	0	|		|	{@GC27@}\n\n{head}Differences from the Standard Code:{head}\n{pre}\n          Code 27        Standard\n\nUAG       Gln            STOP\nUAA       Gln            STOP\nUGA       STOP or Trp    STOP\n\n{pre}\n\n{head}Initiation Codons:{head}\nAUG\n\n{head}Systematic Range:{head}\n\n{b}the karyorelictid ciliate Parduczia{b}\n\n{head}Comments:{head}Code 27 reassigns the UAG and UAA stops to glutamine while UGA can function as either STOP or tryptophan. Code 27 is used for the karyorelictid ciliate Parduczia sp. ({link}{pubmed}27426948{pubmed}Swart et al. 2016{link}).	|	1 	|
47856	|	gencode:28:Condylostoma Nuclear Code:280	|	0	|	0	|		|	{@GC28@}\n\n{head}Differences from the Standard Code:{head}\n{pre}\n          Code 28          Standard\n\nUAA       Gln or STOP      STOP\nUAG       Gln or STOP      STOP\nUGA       Trp or STOP      STOP\n\n{pre}\n\n{head}Initiation Codons: AUG{head}\n\n{head}Systematic Range:{head}\n\n{b}Condylostoma magnum{b}\n\n{head}Comments:{head}Code 28 is used in Condylostoma magnum. The difference to the standard code is that the three stop codons can also be translated as glutamine (UAA, UAG) or tryptophan (UGA), respectively({link}{pubmed} 27426948{pubmed}Swart et al. 2016{link}{link}, {pubmed} 27501944{pubmed}Heaphy et al. 2016{link}).	|	1 	|
47857	|	gencode:29:Mesodinium Nuclear Code:290	|	0	|	0	|		|	{@GC29@}\n\n{head}Differences from the Standard Code:{head}\n{pre}\n          Code 29        Standard\n\nUAA       Tyr            STOP\nUAG       Tyr            STOP\n\n{pre}\n\n{head}Initiation Codons:{head}\nAUG\n\n{head}Systematic Range:{head}\n\n{b}the mesodiniid ciliates Mesodinium and Myrionecta{b}\n\n{head}Comments:{head}Code 29 is used for the haptorid ciliates Mesodinium and Myrionecta. It differs from the standard code in reassigning the stop codons UAA and UAG to Tyrosine. ({link}{pubmed}27501944{pubmed}Heaphy et al. 2016{link}).	|	1 	|
47858	|	gencode:30:Peritrich Nuclear Code:300	|	0	|	0	|		|	{@GC30@}\n\n{head}Differences from the Standard Code:{head}\n{pre}\n          Code 30        Standard\n\nUAA       Glu            STOP\nUAG       Glu            STOP\n\n{pre}\n\n{head}Initiation Codons:{head}\nAUG\n\n{head}Systematic Range:{head}\n\n{b}the peritrich ciliate Carchesium{b}\n\n{head}Comments:{head}Code 30 is used in the peritrich ciliate Carchesium. The stop codons UAA and UAG are reassigned to Glutamine. ({link}{pubmed}12620196{pubmed}Sanchez-Silva et al. 2003{link}).	|	1 	|
47859	|	gencode:31:Blastocrithidia Nuclear Code:310	|	0	|	0	|		|	{@GC31@}\n\n{head}Differences from the Standard Code:{head}\n{pre}\n          Code 31          Standard\n\nUGA       Trp              STOP\nUAG       Glu or STOP      STOP\nUAA       Glu or STOP      STOP\n\n{pre}\n\n{head}Initiation Codons:{head}\nAUG\n\n{head}Systematic Range:{head}\n\n{b}Blastocrithidia sp.{b}\n\n{head}Comments:{head}Code 31 is used for the trypanosome Blastocrithidia sp. UGA encodes trytophan and  UAG and UAA encode glutamate and also serve as termination codons. ({link}{pubmed}27593378{pubmed}Zahonova et al. 2016{link}).	|	1 	|
