57454	|	gencode:33:Cephalodiscidae Mitochondrial UAA-Tyr Code:330	|	0	|	0	|		|	{@GC33@}\n\n{head}Differences from the Standard Code:{head}\n{pre}\n     Code 33     Standard\nUAA  Tyr         STOP\nUGA  Trp         STOP\nAGA  Ser         Arg\nAGG  Lys         Arg\n{pre}\n\n{head}Systematic Range:{head}\nCephalodiscidae (Hemichordata)\n\n{head}Comments:{head}\n\nCode 33 is very similar to the mitochondrial code 24 for the {i}Pterobranchia{i}, which also belong to the {i}Hemichordata{i}, except that it uses UAA for tyrosine rather than as a stop codon ({link}{pubmed}30476024{pubmed}Li Y, Kocot KM, Tassia MG, Cannon JT, Bernt M, Halanych KM. Mitogenomics Reveals a Novel Genetic Code in Hemichordata. Genome Biol Evol. 2019 Jan 1;11(1):29-40.{link})\n	|	1 	|
