57586	|	Herpetomonas samuelpessoai and Herpetomonas pessoai 	|	0	|	0	|		|	Herpetomonas samuelpessoai (Galvao et al. 1970)  Roitman et al. 1976 has been isolated from an assassin bug (Zelus leucogrammus) and originally named Leptomonas pessoai (Galvao et al. 1970). Galvao deposited a culture from the type material of Herpetomonas samuelpessoai at the ATCC (ATCC 30252).  When Roitman et al. 1976 (PMID: 933085) recognized that the species belonged in the genus Herpetomonas, they could not use the combination Herpetomonas pessoai because that was preoccupied by Herpetomonas pessoai Ayroza Galvao & Coutinho, 1941. Roitman et al. 1976 therefore selected a newepithet and renamedLeptomonas pessoai as Herpetomonassamuelpessoai. \nHerpetomonas pessoai has been described by Ayroza Galvao & Coutinho, 1941 from an Anopheles mosquito. No culture or type material is known and it has probably not been studied since the original description.\n	|	5715 2518191 	|
